## Constants & Configuration

### Separate Constants from Types

Constants must be in separate files from type definitions:

```
src/
├── constants/             # All constants here
│   ├── api.constants.ts   # API error codes, HTTP status
│   ├── auth.constants.ts  # Permissions, roles
│   ├── query.constants.ts # Pagination defaults
│   └── index.ts           # Central export
├── types/                 # Pure type definitions (no runtime values)
│   ├── api.types.ts
│   ├── auth.types.ts
│   └── index.ts
```

**Rules:**
- Type files (`*.types.ts`) should contain ONLY types and interfaces
- Constants (`as const` objects, default values) go in `*.constants.ts`
- Export types from constants using `typeof` when needed

```typescript
// constants/api.constants.ts
export const API_ERROR_CODES = {
  VALIDATION_ERROR: 'VALIDATION_ERROR',
  UNAUTHORIZED: 'UNAUTHORIZED',
} as const;

// types/api.types.ts
import { API_ERROR_CODES } from '@/constants';
export type ApiErrorCode = (typeof API_ERROR_CODES)[keyof typeof API_ERROR_CODES];
```

### Separate DTOs by Domain

DTO (Data Transfer Object) types must be organized in separate files by domain:

```
src/types/
├── dto/                      # All DTOs in subdirectory
│   ├── expense.dto.ts        # Expense CRUD, approval DTOs
│   ├── attachment.dto.ts     # File upload DTOs
│   ├── user.dto.ts           # User profile DTOs
│   ├── report.dto.ts         # Report generation DTOs
│   └── index.ts              # Central export
├── api.types.ts
├── auth.types.ts
└── index.ts
```

**Rules:**
- Each domain gets its own `*.dto.ts` file
- DTOs are request/response shapes for API endpoints
- Group related DTOs together (e.g., CreateExpenseDto, UpdateExpenseDto in expense.dto.ts)
- Bulk action DTOs stay with their domain (BulkApproveDto in expense.dto.ts)

```typescript
// types/dto/expense.dto.ts
export interface CreateExpenseDto {
  vendorName: string;
  amount: number;
  // ...
}

export interface ApproveExpenseDto {
  expenseId: string;
  comments?: string;
}
```

### Separate Entity Types by Domain

Entity types (with relations) must be organized in separate files by domain:

```
src/types/
├── entities/                  # All entity types in subdirectory
│   ├── base.entity.ts         # Re-exports from Drizzle schema
│   ├── user.entity.ts         # UserWithTenant, etc.
│   ├── expense.entity.ts      # ExpenseWithRelations, ExpenseSummary, etc.
│   ├── attachment.entity.ts   # ExpenseAttachmentSummary, etc.
│   ├── audit.entity.ts        # AuditTrailEntry, ExpenseChangeRecord
│   └── index.ts               # Central export
├── dto/
├── api.types.ts
└── index.ts
```

**Rules:**
- Base Drizzle types are re-exported from `base.entity.ts`
- Extended types with relations go in domain-specific files
- Summary/list view types stay with their domain entity
- Statistics types stay with their domain entity

```typescript
// types/entities/expense.entity.ts
import type { Expense, User, GlCode } from './base.entity';

export interface ExpenseWithRelations extends Expense {
  submitter: Pick<User, 'id' | 'name' | 'email'>;
  approver?: Pick<User, 'id' | 'name' | 'email'> | null;
  glCode?: Pick<GlCode, 'id' | 'code' | 'description'> | null;
}
```

